+Title: SpaceX — Aegis Pilot: Signed Models, Pre‑Launch Certification, OTA & Evidence for Safety Cases (12 weeks)
+Sponsor: SpaceX Safety / Autonomy / Security
+Duration: 12 weeks
+
+Objective:
+- Prove end‑to‑end cryptographic signing, attestation, human safety approvals, and secure OTA delivery for ML artifacts used by HIL rigs and ground/edge systems. Produce evidence suitable for safety dossiers and incident forensics.
+
+Scope & Deliverables:
+- Dedicated SpaceX-managed tenant / VPC for the pilot (air‑gapped / US‑only).
+- Vault productionization with BYOK/HSM auto‑unseal, Transit key lifecycle & rotation automation.
+- CI templates (OIDC→Vault) to build, sign (Transit/cosign), publish Rekor entry and generate evidence bundles.
+- Rekor production hardening (managed Postgres/RDS, TLS, backups & restore drills).
+- Hardened pre‑load verifier for HIL rigs & edge agents (cosign + Rekor + TPM/TEE).
+- OTA manifest examples (TUF‑style), dual‑partition update script, staged canaries and rollback drills.
+- n8n HIL workflows and incident forensics orchestration integrated with SSO/Slack/PagerDuty.
+- Federated PoC using Flower with poisoning tests and DP post‑aggregation harness (privacy report).
+- Security plan: SCA in CI, pentest scope & remediation workflow.
+
+Timeline & Milestones:
+- Week 0: Kickoff, tenant/VPC provisioning, HSM selection & legal alignment (ITAR/controls).
+- Week 1–3: Vault BYOK/HSM deployment & OIDC roles for CI; sign test artifacts.
+- Week 2–4: Rekor RDS + TLS + backup automation and restore drill.
+- Week 3–6: CI pipeline rollout, evidence bundle attachment to MLflow.
+- Week 5–8: Deploy pre‑load verifier to HIL rigs and test offline verification.
+- Week 6–9: OTA canary & dual‑partition test runs, rollback drill.
+- Week 8–11: Federated PoC rounds, poisoning tests, DP experiments and privacy report.
+- Week 11–12: Pilot wrap, evidence packages for safety/regulatory, lessons learned.
+
+Acceptance Criteria:
+- 100% of pilot artifacts have valid signatures + Rekor entries + evidence bundles in MLflow.
+- Pre‑load verification pass rate = 100% on HIL rigs for signed artifacts.
+- OTA rollback drill completes within target (e.g., < 15 minutes) for representative devices.
+- Federated rounds succeed >95%, DP epsilon/delta documented; poisoning tests logged and defenses validated.
+- SCA enabled in CI and external pentest completed with critical/high remediation or accepted residual risk.
+
+Risks & Mitigations:
+- Key custody: BYOK/HSM, dual control, immediate revocation playbook.
+- Device bricking: dual partition + staged canaries + rollback drills.
+- Regulatory/ITAR: host in SpaceX-managed US-only tenant, legal sign-off before any cross-border flows.
+
+Staffing:
+- SpaceX: Security/HSM lead, Safety/HIL lead, Edge/Vehicle SW, CI/Platform engineers.
+- Aegis: Platform SRE, Security architect, ML/Privacy engineer, Edge engineer.
